  "worked_solution": "We find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nP=2.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=-2,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=-{e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+Q\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)+{e}^{-x}(-P\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+Q\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x).\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=-2$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-P+Q=-2.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $P=2$ gives $Q=0.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
